- Treating a scanner result as automatically exploitable.
- Ignoring false positives or stale software versions.
- Losing the original evidence or tool configuration.
- Using production credentials or secrets in an experimental test.
- Installing arbitrary third-party binaries on a worker.
- Treating a successful security test as permission to attack an external party.

